    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="6.4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:EGu">EGu</ref> 6.4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.4" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="132" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwá ænigra godcundra gerihto<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#EGu_6-4.lnote.oe.3"/> forwyrne, gylde lahslit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#EGu_6-4.lnote.oe.2"/> mid Denu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, wíte mid Englu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.4" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="132" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf hwá ænigra godcundra gerihta forwyrna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#EGu_6-4.lnote.oe.1"/>, gylde lahslitt mid Denu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, wite mid Englum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="133" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis Dei rectitudines aliquas difforciat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#EGu_6-4.lnote.oe.5"/>, reddat lahslit cum Dacis, witam cum Anglis.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="6.4" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="104" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif hwá ænigra godcundra gerihto forwyrne<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#EGu_6-4.attnote.fn.19"/>, gylde lahslit mid Denum, wíte mid Englum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="6" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif hwa ænigra godcundra gerihto forwyrne, gylde lahslit mid Denum, wite mid Englum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="133" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#EGu_6-4.lnote.de.1"/> jemand irgend welche kirchlichen Gerechtsame<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#EGu_6-4.lnote.de.2"/> verweigert<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#EGu_6-4.lnote.de.3"/>, zahle er Rechtsbruchbusse bei den Dänen, Strafgeld bei den Engländern.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If anyone refuses any of the Church’s dues, let him pay the penalty for breach of law among the Danes, a fine among the English.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="105" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone refuses [to render] any church dues, he shall pay <hi rend="italic">lahslit</hi> in a Danish district, and a fine in an English district.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="7" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone withholds his Church dues, he shall pay lahslit among the Danes or a penalty among the English.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_48">II Cn 48</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_48">II Cn 48–48.3</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 48-48:3: EGu 6:4-7</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="391"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Grith_13">Grið 13–14</ref> <quote>But the question of the Church's security from attack was precisely the concern of 'Edward–Guthrum''s first clause, and is probably behind a pair of clauses about assaults on clergy</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_6-4.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">133</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">disforciet <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">disforciet TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_6-4.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ta <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ta Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_6-4.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ite <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ite Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_6-4.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_6-4.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dieser Satz bedeutet, im Ggs. zu 6, 5, kampflose Weigerung; beides verschmilzt unklarer II Cn 48. 48, 1 (daraus Hn 11, 11—c). Dieser droht <hi rend="italic">fulwite</hi>, d. i., laut Zwölfereid, 120 Schill. Strafgeld</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This sentence means, in contrast to 6, 5, refusal without fighting; II Cn 48. 48, 1 (whence Hn 11, 11—c) merges the two less clearly. It threatens <hi rend="italic">fulwite</hi>, i.e., according to the Twelve-hynde oath, a fine of 120 shill.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_6-4.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wie 5, 1, doch mit Strafdrohung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">As 5, 1, but with a threat of punishment</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_6-4.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu -<hi rend="italic">a</hi> in <hi rend="italic">forwyrna s. Wb</hi> 39 Sp. 1 Z. 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On -<hi rend="italic">a</hi> in <hi rend="italic">forwyrna see Wb</hi> 39 col. 1 l. 13</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="EGu_6-4.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope></bibl><label>forwyrne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gerihta forwyrna</hi>. B.</seg></note>
      </div>
